{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style","id":1233320,"title":"How to update Falling Blossom Style?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-08T18:54:15-07:00","id":1233320,"title":"How to update Falling Blossom Style?","content":"What sort of bare-handed striking techniques are appropriate for this Style? Should it include grappling techniques at all?<br /> <br /> Knives are an excellent weapon, because of how easy they are for caretakers and bodyguards to casually carry for defense at a moment's notice, and how easy they are to conceal for defense in situations where others expect them to disarm.<br /> <br /> Swords were part of this Style in Second Edition, but no mention is made of what <i>kind</i> of swords. Further, there's no particular reason why swords are more appropriate than other weapons. Why not spears or axes?<br /> <br /> Shields have been excluded from this Style in the past, which sort of makes sense mechanically in that shields are primarily about Rushing or Disengaging while flurrying a Full Defense action for a net gain of +1 Defense, which doesn't by itself help with Defend Other actions. Using a shield also runs counter to the &quot;exposing yourself to death to protect someone else's life&quot; theme, though shields ought to be thematically appropriate for protecting someone else from harm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Charms, this Style would definitely need a few new ones, based in themes of blood and protection.<br /> <br /> Like, the more blood your chosen ward has lost, the more powerful your weapon becomes.<br /> <br /> Or, the blood you lose becomes animated as a magical shield that protects your ward, and if you die, the shield becomes even stronger.<br /> <br /> With a new pinnacle Charm that allows you to sacrifice all of your remaining health in order to heal your ward; if this kills you, the blood shield's full power is triggered.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lioness had an excellent idea in the form of a Charm that allows a Falling Blossom martyr to tie up all opponents in close range so that they cannot contest the Disengage action of the ward. The Mastery level of this Charm would allow the ward to Disengage reflexively.<br /> <br /> Since the game now includes the Defend Other action in the basic rules, with native Exalted Charms empowering the action in various ways, Lioness' idea might be used in the updated version of Living Shield Technique.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unlike Crane and Melee-based Defend Other Charms or Dodge Charms, which allow you to freely defend anyone you please at the drop of a hat, this Style might have a particular focus on defending ONE specific individual whom is the subject of a strong Intimacy, with the Charms behaving more powerfully in response to a more intense Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any other thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T21:13:20-07:00","id":1233332,"title":"","content":"The disengage charm as the form charm is going to be pretty weak against exalts. Any charm, like thunderclap rush, that lets you move automatically breaks disengage with no penality. I'd probably focus on stripping initiative when attacking the ward or when running away from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T21:23:53-07:00","id":1233334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233332#post1233332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disengage charm as the form charm is going to be pretty weak against exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say anything about the form Charm. I mentioned the disengage trick in relation to Living Shield Technique, which is one of the pre-form Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T23:55:33-07:00","id":1233354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233332#post1233332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any charm, like thunderclap rush, that lets you move automatically breaks disengage with no penality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thunderclap Rush Attack doesn't let you move for free; it uses up your move action for the turn, and thus doesn't automatically break disengage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T00:53:46-07:00","id":1233362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233354#post1233354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thunderclap Rush Attack doesn't let you move for free; it uses up your move action for the turn, and thus doesn't automatically break disengage.</div> </div> </div> </div> It explicitly lets you move and attack without using a move action and out of turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 07-09-2018, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T05:44:07-07:00","id":1233386,"title":"","content":"To me &quot;immediately and re\ufb02exively retreats&quot; is unambiguous enough that I'd expect a charm that lets you close in on them and attack them before that can take place to be abundantly clear. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T05:48:23-07:00","id":1233389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233332#post1233332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disengage charm as the form charm is going to be pretty weak against exalts. Any charm, like thunderclap rush, that lets you move automatically breaks disengage with no penality. I'd probably focus on stripping initiative when attacking the ward or when running away from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the confusion, now. I used the word \u201cform\u201d to refer to the shape of Lioness\u2019 idea for a Charm. I was not referring to the Form Charm of the Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T05:58:44-07:00","id":1233393,"title":"","content":"Regarding swords as form weapons, I think they make sense, both pragmatically and symbolically. <br /> <br /> Pragmatically, swords have a number of qualities that make them practical for bodyguards. They tend to be better at defense than other similarly sized weapons. Axes and blunt weapons tend to be top-heavy to generate more momentum with each swing, which in turn reduces their maneuverability when defending. Swords are weighted for maximum maneuverability and also come with all sorts of handy defensive features like the hand guard. They're also pretty flexible in their usage compared to other weapons. They can cut, they can stab, they can disarm, they can be used as a leverage to knock enemies down, you can grab one by the blade and bash the enemy over the head with a pommel or quillions - lots of uses for a bar of steel! Since bodyguards need to be able to fight off all kinds of possible threats to their ward, an adaptable weapon with good defensive capabilities is a reasonable choice.<br /> <br /> Symbolically, swords are often seen as a high-class weapon, to the point where some cultures only let nobles carry them. Since only people of high social status get to employ bodyguards, you want bodyguards to fit a high-status setting without sticking out like a sore thumb, so equipping them with a high-status weapon seems logical. At the same time, with very few exceptions, swords are strictly &quot;sidearms&quot;, i.e. weapons you can still carry around in a non-military setting without drawing too much attention.<br /> <br /> On a slightly more philosophical note, I've heard a theory somewhere that the high status of the sword was due to the fact that unlike most weapons which had their roots in various hunting and/or farming tools, and could conceivably serve some non-combat needs, the sword was solely designed for fighting and killing humans. I can see this symbolism being important to Falling Blossom practitioners, always equally ready to take and give life in service to their ward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T06:31:23-07:00","id":1233405,"title":"","content":"Good points, but what kind of swords?<br /> <br /> I always pictured double-edged straight swords, as opposed to chopping, thrusting, or slashing swords. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what about armor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T06:42:40-07:00","id":1233408,"title":"","content":"The martyr should be ready to fight at a moment\u2019s notice without any armor at all, but if the bodyguard and his ward are deliberately going into battle, the bodyguard can prepare. If they are going not specifically into battle, but traveling outside of a protected home or into the lawless wilderness, the bodyguard could at least prepare with medium armor, and in the home itself the bodyguard would likely always be wearing light armor.<br /> <br /> Obvious armor is as useful as concealed armor. Concealment for surprise or infiltration, but blatant armor as a deterrent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T10:51:53-07:00","id":1233470,"title":"","content":"After thinking about it, this Style is a natural fit for some basic grappling, as clinching an enemy hinders their efforts to attack your ward or contest her disengage action. Also, knives and clinches go together like zealotry and martyrdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T18:15:25-07:00","id":1233560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233470#post1233470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After thinking about it, this Style is a natural fit for some basic grappling, as clinching an enemy hinders their efforts to attack your ward or contest her disengage action. Also, knives and clinches go together like zealotry and martyrdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clinching and grappling only make sense in a 1v1 situation. Which limits it's application if you wish to protect someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T18:22:54-07:00","id":1233562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233560#post1233560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clinching and grappling only make sense in a 1v1 situation. Which limits it's application if you wish to protect someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will be plenty of times where you only need to defend your ward against a single attacker, and that makes it worthwhile for the Ability to be applicable to grappling.<br /> <br /> For the other times, yes, a Defend Other action is a wiser idea than a grappling gambit.<br /> <br /> <br /> On that note, I'm having trouble thinking of pre-Form Charms that don't include a reskin of Fluttering Cry of Warning. Which is not to say that I don't have ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T02:46:32-07:00","id":1233933,"title":"","content":"I think the style's pre-form charms could update fine and three of them is a decent number. It's the post-form part of the style that is a bit light and where I feel we go from fanatically loyal bodyguard to disposable NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T04:55:34-07:00","id":1233949,"title":"","content":"I always looked at the trappings of Fallen Blossom as invoking the yojimbo, the Hagakure's teachings on living in service to ones master as if already dead and therefore willing to give their life at a moment's notice for them. Based on that I feel it'd be remiss to exclude slashing swords. The least fitting in my mind would be great swords; chopping does khopesh, straight for gladius and knightly swords. Further commented by the above arguments about the sword as a symbol of noble office and rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T06:11:36-07:00","id":1233965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1233320-how-to-update-falling-blossom-style?p=1233933#post1233933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the style's pre-form charms could update fine and three of them is a decent number. It's the post-form part of the style that is a bit light and where I feel we go from fanatically loyal bodyguard to disposable NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Undefended Assault Method is basically a Clash attack you should be able to use to Clash an attack against your ward, and Dual Scarlet Blossom Technique should be a proper Counterattack, and both of those tricks have always been post-Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T11:12:07-07:00","id":1234050,"title":"","content":"Conceptually speaking, I wonder if it would be possible to have a special keyword on a couple of the base charms that allowed mortal practitioners to learn and use them by spending lots of health levels. That might make the style too strong, I dunno. But it would reward the whole \u201cfanatically devoted bodyguard pushing themselves to death to protect someone\u201d thing with a bit of power and tie back in to the style\u2019s mystique, but in a way that Exalted don\u2019t have to emulate. So you could have a Falling Blossom Stylist who exalted performing the Cherry Petal Sacrifice (or whatever you want to call it), unexpectedly survives, and still gets plenty of use out of the charms without needing to kill themselves over it.<br /> <br /> Maybe a special Merit, like the ones you get from Sorcerous Initation? <br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe a custom gambit or special maneuver, akin to Wood stylists being able to use a bow as a staff, that lets them spend health levels on something. Maybe reduce the flurry penalty for attacking while Defend Othering or let them make a decisive counterattack if someone attacks their ward.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they can take a penalty to defense while using Defend Other, but in exchange anyone attacking their ward has to attack them first. Or maybe reduce their defense to zero, but they get a decisive counterattack against the attacker. <br /> <br /> Hmmm.... I haven\u2019t really looked at the clash mechanics. Could a normal person hold their action to clash someone that had a lower init total? What about allowing stylists to flurry a Defend Other and a Clash attack, even if the Clash happened later in the turn, at a penalty to defense and/or health level cost? That might work a lot better than a non charm counterattack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 07-11-2018, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T11:59:51-07:00","id":1234062,"title":"","content":"The original idea of this Style involved a mortal throwing themselves at their ward\u2019s enemy without a thought to defense until one of them died, with the occasional leap back to the ward to shield them from harm.<br /> <br /> Literally the only protective Charm is Living Shield Technique. Everything else is about killing yourself to killl your ward\u2019s target, who needs no defense from a dead man.<br /> <br /> <br /> Living Shield Technique today would be more powerful than Crane Style\u2019s pre-Form Fluttering Cry of Warning, which only allows a reflexive Defend Other action if you\u2019re a Solar.<br /> <br /> This is because Dragon-Blooded are not supposed to get as many full actions per turn as Solars. They don\u2019t get stuff like War Lion Stance for reflexive Defend Other actions with unflurried attacks, or counterattacks when not taking Defend Other actions.<br /> <br /> Living Shield Technique cannot be allowed to create actions from nothing for anyone but Solars, so I don\u2019t see how Falling Blossom Style can work. Anyone but Solars has to commit to attacking or defending each turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T09:34:35-07:00","id":1234308,"title":"","content":"I just so happen to have updated Falling Blossom Style for 3rd edition:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/13567215/chapters/31169112\" target=\"_blank\">Here, in my Lunar Castebooks.</a><br /> <br /> But, a quick dump with poor formatting for convenience:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><u><b>Falling Blossom Style</b></u><br /> The Falling Blossom stylist is selfish. She knows this in her soul, even if no one ever describes her as such. She wants to be outlived, and she will not hear the people in her life tell her otherwise. To watch the suffering of her loved ones hurts more than fists or knives or sickness. So she chooses the lesser hurt.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Falling Blossom stylist is selfless. She interposes herself between her loved ones and harm, physically and metaphysically. To be loved by a Falling Blossom stylist is to know protection. To fight with one is to know sacrifice. To watch one die protecting her charge is to hear the last chord of a song, to experience the last line in a poem. It is a finality completely fitting the life the Falling Blossom lived.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">All of this is accomplished unarmored - the better to quickly be where the Falling Blossom is needed. A knife or sword can aid in parrying and striking, and this style can also be practiced unarmed. While not strictly required to learn the Charms, a close friend or other loved one nearby makes many of the effects of Falling Blossom Style most effective, and students of this style often seek its power with a special someone in mind.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Style Weapons: Unarmed, knives, short swords<br /> Style Armor: Unarmored only</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Living Shield Technique<br /> Cost: 1m<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 1, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual, Obvious<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The ward of a Falling Blossom who is executing a Defend Other action (3e page 196) supplemented by this Charm is more fully protected than by a simple bodyguard. When an attacker manages to inflict damage through a Falling Blossom\u2019s Defend Other (using the parry derived from their Falling Blossom Ability), the attacker\u2019s damage must target the guardian (either Initiative or Health Levels).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The strike may still land on the ward, but the wound opens on the Falling Blossom. This is the first technique of the Falling Blossom, and it sets the tone for all to come. Sacrifice, defense, protection. Even when the Falling Blossom\u2019s strength of arm fails, their spirit still defends what they care for, what they live for, what they die for.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Undefended Assault Method<br /> Cost: 7m<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-only, Perilous, Mastery<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: Living Shield Technique</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Falling Blossom does not consider whether she will live or die in battle. All of that concern is focused on others. When they see a source of harm aimed at something they love, eliminating the threat becomes paramount. A Falling Blossom may use Undefended Assault Method when attacking with a form weapon (unarmed or wielding a knife or sword) to sacrifice all of her defense to gain that many automatic successes on a withering strike roll. Treat this loss of defense as an onslaught penalty, removed normally on the Falling Blossom\u2019s next action. If another effect cancels or reduces this loss of defense at the time of the strike, then successes are gained only equal to the defense lost. Later changes to the Falling Blossom\u2019s defense are ignored - by then the strike is in the past, just like the combat advantage of the threat to their loved ones.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mastery: The first success gained from Undefended Assault Method is a non-Charm success.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Dual Scarlet Blossom Technique<br /> Cost: 1+m<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Terrestrial<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: Living Shield Technique</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Blood calls to blood. The Falling Blossom knows this in her soul, as her charge\u2019s blood feels like her own, hurting her as much or more when she sees it spilled. With this Charm, it is. Any significant wound sprouts blood or blossoms bruises from them both.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">When the Falling Blossom joins battle she may call out with her spirit to someone she holds dear. She may spend motes up to the intensity of that Intimacy (None: 1, Minor: 2, Major: 3, Defining: 4, 3e Core page 170), binding her blood with her charge\u2019s so long as the battle lasts and the motes are committed.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">When her charge takes 2 or more health levels of damage from any source, such as a single decisive attack, falling damage, or even self-harm to power Charms or other effects, the damage is split between the Falling Blossom and her charge. The Falling Blossom takes half, rounded up, of the damage meant for her charge, to a limit of damage taken by the Falling Blossom equal to the motes committed. The charge\u2019s damage taken is reduced by the amount taken (ignoring any prevented) by the Falling Blossom.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Terrestrial: This Charm cannot fill the Terrestrial\u2019s Incapacitated health level. It simply fails, soaking as much damage as it can prior to the Incapacitated health level, then dropping the mote commitment, and the Falling Blossom cannot share damage any more via this or any other Falling Blossom Style Charm for the scene even if they somehow regain health levels. A Terrestrial user cannot make the ultimate sacrifice with this Charm, instead they are doomed to watch their loved ones fall as their technique fails.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Falling Blossom Form<br /> Cost: 10m<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Form, Mastery, Terrestrial<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Pre-requisites: Dual Scarlet Blossom Technique, Undefended Assault Method</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Falling Blossom does not fall until she sees safe those who need her protection. This armor of belief can delay the bodily injuries she takes in battle. While this Charm is active delay the consequences of a Falling Blossom\u2019s incapacitated health level being filled long as any Intimacy of hers is still under threat in the battle, and ignore any damage that would exceed their incapacitated health level(s). Further, they ignore wound penalties to Defense while Defending Other (3e page 196) up to the highest intensity of the Intimacy they have for the one(s) being defended. She can only weaken and die once she has fulfilled her duty. When the Form drops or when none of her Intimacies are under threat, apply any consequences of their incapacitated health levels as they stand at that moment.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Terrestrial: If an incapacitated health level fills during battle and is delayed by this Charm, they suffer the effects of that incapacitated health level (usually unconsciousness for bashing, death for lethal or aggravated) when this Charm ends even if they have somehow erased that damage in the interim.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mastery: At Essence 3+ the Duration increases to Indefinite. The Falling Blossom who chooses to devote herself to this Charm may only be killed with violence when she is separated from any who she loves.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Purity of Purpose Attack<br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Destiny-only, Mastery<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Pre-requisites: Falling Blossom Form</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Falling Blossom knows what she is meant to do in life. Eliminating her target is either fulfilling that destiny or stopping someone from derailing it. As a special activation rule, the Falling Blossom may only use this Charm when furthering a Destiny background she knows of (such as striking an assailant that has targeted someone she is destined to protect). Decisive strike attacks with a form weapon supplemented by Purity of Purpose Attack automatically succeed.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Any practitioner that cannot have the Destiny Background (Scroll of the Monk page 151) may use this Charm to target a foe who has threatened or harmed one of her Intimacies.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mastery: The masters of this style make their own destinies. Ignore the Destiny-only keyword of this Charm and its special activation rule when a master uses Purity of Purpose Attack.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Strength of Faith Meditation<br /> Cost: -<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Mastery<br /> Duration: -<br /> Pre-requisites: Falling Blossom Form</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Falling Blossom can channel their devotion to ignore their weaknesses in more situations than desperate attempts to defend their charge. Strength of Faith Meditation, once learned, permanently alters the wound penalty reduction of Falling Blossom Form. With Strength of Faith Meditation\u2019s enhancement, ignore wound penalties to all actions so long as any Intimacy of hers is under threat in the scene, using the highest such Intensity for the limits.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mastery: At Essence 4+, the penalty reduction can apply to any die or static value reduction (poisons, crippling injuries, blindness, onslaught, other situational penalties), not just wound penalties. Masters may explicitly and specifically exempt this from applying to the Purity of Purpose Attack onslaught penalty (while still ignoring other onslaught penalties) when they activate Falling Blossom Form enhanced by Strength of Faith Meditation.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Charm Name: Verse of the Martyr<br /> Cost: -<br /> Minimums: Martial Arts (Falling Blossom) 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Mastery<br /> Duration: -<br /> Pre-requisites: Strength of Faith Meditation, Purity of Purpose Attack</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">When learning this Charm, the Falling Blossom composes a poem to a single person who she most wants to live on in this life. Their soul is so perfect, they do not want to live in a world where the other does not also live. As a special activation rule, this Charm can only target living beings, not undead or ghosts. When the target\u2019s incapacitated health level would be filled with lethal or aggravated damage, instead inflict enough damage to fill all the Falling Blossom\u2019s health levels including incapacitated with that type of damage, regardless of distance or awareness. The entire attack strikes through the target of the verse, hitting the Falling Blossom instead, ignoring any effect on the original target. If a non-violent death should befall the Fallen Blossom\u2019s target, that fate instead switches places, fully curing the target of all effects associated with that death (such as sickness, restoring them to health, or old age, restoring them to youth) while the Fallen Blossom falls in their place should she not have some way to save herself from that particular malady. Unlike other Charms of this style, the target of the verse is spared even if the Martyr has some way to survive the harm they have taken on.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mastery: The Solar and Abyssal Falling Blossoms can write numerous verses, each targeting a different soul. Targets up to the master\u2019s Essence may know protection under the magnanimity of the sun, or a pardon from Lethe and Oblivion. Sidereal Falling Blossoms cannot usually use this Charm to take the death themselves, and can only write the verse for one target, but they can find up to their Essence in threads that are so similar to their target that their poetry confuses the two strands in the Loom of Fate - when the target would die another similar thread is cut instead. When that condition triggers, they take Paradox equal to the target\u2019s Essence, as the pattern spiders are incensed at the deliberate miscalibration of causality.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 07-13-2018, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T06:00:35-07:00","id":1235878,"title":"","content":"I guess I killed the thread? Any feedback would be appreciated. Terrible, awesome, kinda meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}